
FAMECfgTest is a simple test program which tests nearly every possible
FAME Config data structure loading of the FAME Config feature.

There are various functions which will request a data structure depending
on what the function has been written for and they will also be used
to release the data structures. Called with 0 as argument they obtain
and with 1 the release the data structure.

The main function calls most of the functions and prompts between.
If everything has been obtained erverything will be released then
between prompts. You can break the tool anytime. Don't worry if
you break FAMECfgTest and the FAMECfgTest hasn't released data structures,
because there is no further check which releases on a shutdown.
In this case you just simply need to wuit every FAME.library using
program and flush the layers by typing "avail flush" in a shell.
Now the FAME.library will be flushed and all data structure memory
will be released and if modified saved first. Or live with the
not released data structures if you don't want or if you don't can
flush yet. It does not harm FAME or the system. The memory of this
data strcutures just couldn'only be freed automatically if no using
tool is left for it, because the opencounter of it is still > 0.

The user data depending structures are disabled. Not because they
arn't working. I just don't wanted them in the code on my last test ;)

